{-
   Assigning a `&` window parameter as a whole, and a borrow into storage that owns.

   collections.md gives `&xs: [a]` "elements mutable, extent fixed": the window is the caller's
   elements, so `v = copy(w)` released the caller's array and wrote an owner where a descriptor was
   (the caller then read a length of five billion), and `v = v[0..1]` was an internal error. The
   bounds facts (J189) key a window parameter's length once per call on the same promise. Element
   writes stay legal - `fill` below is accepted.

   And a borrow assigned into a field that owns its array, reached through a `&` parameter: the
   field's own contract decides, not the unique borrow it was reached through, so it is the ordinary
   "`copy` it" refusal rather than "store consumes a guaranteed value".
-}

data Box {bytes: [U8]}

fn fill(&v: [U8]):
    for i in 0..length(v):
        v[i] = 7

fn shrinkOwned(&v: '[U8]):
    let w = v[0..1]
    v = copy(w)

fn shrinkView(&v: '[U8]):
    v = v[0..1]

fn replaceOut(&out: [U8], view: [U8]):
    out = view[1..length(view)]

fn setField(&b: Box, view: [U8]):
    b.bytes = view[1..length(view)]
